  ('lib-001b6fa9899b84d3a84e5370', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Move one time, move them all', '4:40 p.m. The bride is twenty minutes late. ⤵
The caterer, the band and the emcee still have the old times.

You start calling. The caterer first, because the food can''t wait. Then the band, who are already tuning. Then the emcee, who is about to announce an entrance that isn''t happening yet. By the time you reach the photographer, the time has moved again, and the caterer is calling you back.

One delay is never one delay. It''s five, unless everyone hears it at once.

On Setnayan, you shift the schedule when you run late: move one moment, and every supplier''s time moves with it. And time changes go through the coordinator. A supplier can propose a new time; you decide. Nobody moves alone, and nobody works from yesterday''s run-of-show.

One habit that helps even without an app: name a single time-keeper for the day, and tell every supplier in the brief that a time only changes when that person says so.

