  ('lib-688b1e79f6524be958cfc59c', 'Problems of a Coordinator · One running order for everyone', '''Run-of-show v7 FINAL final.pdf'' Sent in four chats. ⤵
The lights team is still working from v5.

Every forward is a new copy, and only one copy is right. By the night before, you''ve stopped knowing which suppliers have which version, and the first sign of trouble is the band setting up where the cake table goes.

On Setnayan, every booked supplier has their own desk inside the event''s Event Hub. Before the day it''s their call sheet: the venue, the running order, the headcount and their own tools. On the day it''s the same desk, current. Nobody opens an old file, because there''s no file to forward.

Even before you use any app, try this on your next event: send the run-of-show once, as one link, and update what''s behind the link instead of sending a new file. Ask suppliers to delete the old PDFs. It feels strange the first time. By the third event, nobody asks ''which version po?''

