  ('lib-7074d87442fa221412189ebe', 'Problems of a Coordinator · In every supplier chat', '''Ay, nag-usap na po kami ng caterer.'' Two weeks before the wedding. ⤵
The menu changed. You find out at the tasting.

Nobody meant to leave you out. The couple messaged the caterer directly, the way couples do, and adding you never came up. Now your setup times, the kitchen space and the serving plan are built on a menu that no longer exists.

On Setnayan, once you''re the event''s booked coordinator, you''re in every supplier chat. You can''t be left out of a supplier conversation, so the menu change lands in front of you the moment it''s made. You see the event and the chats; the hosts still decide, and only hosts book or pay.

The habit that works anywhere: in your first meeting with the couple, ask one thing out loud. ''Please add me to every supplier chat, from today, even the ones you''ve already started.'' Then check, one supplier at a time, that it happened.

