  ('lib-5378831b8b73779eb32afd5a', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Start with three numbers', 'They arrive with a 40-page Pinterest board. ⤵
No guest count. No budget. Three possible dates.

The first meeting is where a coordinator earns trust, and it''s easy to lose it by planning everything at once. A list of a hundred tasks feels thorough to you and terrifying to them.

Start with three numbers, written together: a guest-count range, a budget range, two or three dates. Then send them home with one job for the week.

On Setnayan, once you''re the event''s booked coordinator, you open the hosts'' own event: their Today list, their checklist, their guests. And every client''s event sits side by side in one login, soonest first, each showing what needs you. You see what they see, so the next meeting starts from the same page. The hosts still decide everything; you just stop guessing what they''ve already done, and they stop repeating it.

