  ('lib-a8027dfa59f18dfe8f7b7534', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Pending holds the seat', 'Two weeks out. 38 guests haven''t answered. ⤵
The venue wants a final count. Tita wants seats for three more cousins. You can''t guess.

On Setnayan, pending guests keep their seats until a person releases them. Nobody gets dropped by a timer they didn''t know about. When a guest says no, their seat opens by itself, and the meal count follows.

That changes your job. You don''t chase the whole list, only who''s still pending, and the live count shows you exactly who: attending, pending, maybe, declined.

Then agree a cut-off date with the hosts. On that date, release the seats still pending, and offer them to the cousins on the waiting list. The rule is the hosts'', the record is clear, and nobody''s seat vanishes by accident. And if a pending guest finally answers yes after the cut-off, you''ll see it in the count straight away.

