  ('lib-fe63d97f6bd5a42d31439424', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Let the parent read the quote', 'You sent your quote. ''Seen,'' 9:14 p.m. Then nothing for six days. ⤵
They didn''t ghost you. They''re waiting for Mama.

In many Filipino families, the couple asks the supplier, but a parent decides, or pays, or both. So the quote you sent is read by someone who can''t say yes yet. It gets screenshotted, forwarded, explained over dinner, and the reply waits for a family meeting you''ll never see.

Following up harder doesn''t speed that up. Getting the quote in front of the person deciding does.

On Setnayan, the couple can add a parent as a co-host. Co-hosts plan with them and are in the supplier chat, so the parent reads the same quote card you sent: every line, the valid-until date and the payment plan. Nobody has to forward a screenshot of a screenshot, and the question that''s holding things up can come to you directly.

