The 18 roses, 18 candles and 18 treasures are the most rehearsed part of a debut, and the most edited. Every swap is a name the emcee has to read right, in front of everyone.

The trouble is copies. A list printed on Monday is wrong by Thursday, and nobody knows which copy is the latest.

On Setnayan, debut rosters (roses, candles, treasures and more) are built into the event''s setup and its run of show. As the booked coordinator, you can edit the schedule, so a swap is made once, in the running order everyone opens. Booked suppliers see that running order on their desk inside the Event Hub, so the emcee and the host aren''t working from a forwarded photo.

A habit that helps either way: agree a cut-off day with the family. After it, every change comes through you.

