  ('lib-283eb310370036fa6c88f5e6', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Your access ends 7 days after', 'Scroll your phone. How many old clients'' guest lists are still on it? ⤵
Names, mobile numbers, table plans, from events that ended a year ago.

Nobody keeps them on purpose. They pile up in downloads, chats and shared sheets, and every one holds the numbers of people who never met you.

On Setnayan, a coordinator''s access to a client''s event closes on its own, 7 days after the event. That''s a week for the thank-yous, the supplier follow-ups and your own notes. The hosts keep their event for good; you don''t carry their family''s data around.

If you''ll want something later, like the timing notes for your own records, write it into your files during that week. After it, the event is the family''s again.

A habit that helps either way: today, delete one old client''s guest list. Keep your notes, not their numbers.

