Livestreams rarely fail because the technology is hard. They fail because nobody owns them: a cousin''s laptop, the venue''s Wi-Fi and a link sent in three different chats.

On Setnayan, every event gets a free one-camera livestream on its Event Hub, for family who can''t come. It needs a laptop at the venue with free streaming software. And because it''s on the Event Hub, the family abroad finds it on the same link they already have.

What helps most is a name: one stream owner, one laptop, a test two days before, and a wired line if the venue has one. Tell the family abroad the start time in their own time zone, so Lola isn''t waiting since noon.

