  ('lib-3d3c7f922e6e601d2f3f12c2', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Let guests opt out of the wall', 'The photo wall is the hit of the night. Then a guest''s face comes up, and she looks away. ⤵
She never wanted to be on it. She''d never have said so.

Guests have their reasons: someone who left a hard situation, someone who shouldn''t be seen at a certain place, someone who simply hates photos. At a live photo wall, they can''t control what''s shown, and most won''t ask the host to change anything at their event.

On Setnayan, every guest can opt out with FaceBlock, from their own pass, without asking anyone. Opted-out guests are blurred everywhere, venue screens included. It costs nothing, and it''s never sold. And only photos that pass a safety screen reach the wall at all.

For the host, it means the wall can stay on, and nobody has to feel trapped by it.

