  ('lib-7c3d5e393aef36c66a5646f8', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Put the crew meal on the quote', 'Your photographer works 12 hours. Your coordinator, ten. The band, six. ⤵
Who feeds them? Usually nobody wrote it down.

Crew meals are one of those costs that live in nobody''s contract. The host assumes the supplier eats before. The supplier assumes the host will feed the crew, the way most events do. Then at 8 p.m. there are nine hungry people at the service door and a caterer counting plates that were never ordered.

It''s not a big cost. It''s an unwritten one, and unwritten costs become arguments.

The fix is simple: put it on the quote. On Setnayan a quote is an itemised card in the chat, so a supplier can add a line like "Crew meals: 4 pax, provided by host" and the host sees it before saying yes. Same for the caterer: "Crew meals, 9 plates" is a line, not a surprise.

