  ('lib-851821cc30069d1fc578d4f0', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Church and reception, one schedule', 'The baptism is at 10. There are six other babies. The reception caterer was told 11. ⤵
The church sets the clock, not you.

Group baptisms run on the parish''s schedule, and the real time sink is the gap: photos at the font, the drive, the parking. Plan that gap as its own moment, and tell the caterer the reception start with that buffer in.

