  ('lib-f0e67e1401cd41f6c8fe504e', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Write the rain plan down', 'Everyone has a rain plan. Usually it''s in one person''s head. ⤵
Then it rains, and that person is fixing the bride''s veil.

A real rain plan answers three questions: where do we move, who decides, and by what time. If those answers aren''t written where the coordinator, the caterer and the lights crew can see them, the plan is a hope.

On Setnayan, the schedule holds the day''s moments, so the rain plan can be one of them: "4:00 p.m., move the ceremony to the function hall if it''s raining · decided by the coordinator." If it pushes everything back, shift everything: move one moment and every supplier''s time moves with it. And guests opening their own link to find their seat see the running schedule there too.

