  ('lib-632d8fa0a12f894c36faaac9', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Your price, on a card', 'Flat fee or a percentage of the event budget? ⤵
Coordinators argue this one every year. Hosts just want to know the number.

A percentage grows with the event, which feels fair on a big wedding but is hard for a host to predict while the budget is still moving. A flat fee is easy to say yes to, as long as the scope is clear: how many meetings, which suppliers you handle, how many hours on the day.

Whichever you choose, write the inclusions next to the price. On Setnayan, a service card can''t go online without a cover photo, a starting price and what''s included. You can make one card for full coordination and another for day-of only, each with its own price. And once you''re verified (free), your cards show up when hosts search.

A clear price is the first sign of a clear coordinator.

