  ('lib-22abbdf6ef7ba08c26e8d741', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · A booking needs a yes', '"Seen 2:14 p.m." Is that a yes? ⤵
To the couple, maybe. To you, it''s nothing yet.

A lot of booking trouble starts in this grey zone. The couple thinks they''ve booked because the supplier saw the message. The supplier thinks nothing is booked until money moves. Both of them plan around a booking that only one of them believes in.

On Setnayan, the grey zone has a button. A couple presses Lock on your quote, and that asks you to book. Your yes is what makes the booking, and you have 48 hours to answer. If another couple is already waiting on you for that date, or the date is full, the app asks you to answer them first or refuses the second yes.

So a booking isn''t a feeling in a chat. It''s a question and an answer both sides can see.

