  ('lib-a9a14dceb0cdd15bcd0d42c9', 'Problems of a Coordinator · One list for every add-on', 'Photo booth, livestream, same-day video, a photo wall. ⤵
Every add-on is a small supplier with its own power, space and timing.

Add-ons fail in the same two places: power and signal. The booth needs outlets near the dance floor. The livestream needs a connection that holds. And each add-on needs a time slot and a contact person, or they all ask the coordinator at once.

Make one list before the day: who brings it, where it plugs in, when it runs, who answers for it. Then check signal and outlets at the ocular, not on the day.

On Setnayan, the guests'' own photos don''t need a booth or an app: with Papic, guests point at a code and shoot, and every photo lands in one album. If the venue has no signal, photos save on the phone and send when it''s back. Every event also includes a free one-camera livestream on the Event Hub (bring a laptop).

