  ('lib-1382bc8b8638bed5a457264e', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Remind the hosts. Never pay.', '"Ma''am, wala pa po yung balance ng client ninyo." ⤵
The supplier asks the coordinator. The coordinator asks the hosts. The hosts ask, "Para saan ulit yun?"

Most coordinators learn this rule the hard way: remind, but never handle the money. A coordinator who collects or pays on the client''s behalf becomes part of every payment dispute that follows.

On Setnayan, a coordinator sees every supplier''s payments due in the event''s budget, view only. One tap, Remind the hosts, sends them a reminder. The coordinator can''t log or pay, by design. And when the hosts pay, the supplier marks it received or not received, with both records kept, so "nag-send na po ako" has an answer.

Put the same rule in your contract: who pays, who reminds, and how a payment is confirmed. It protects your client, the supplier and you, and it keeps you on the side of the event, not the side of the money.

Coordinators, do you ever handle client payments?

