  ('lib-d961f02705566bdfdf9b920d', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · The booked price stays', 'You raised your rates for 2027. Fair: your costs went up, your work got better. ⤵
Then a couple who booked you last October messages: ''Ma''am, affected po ba kami?''

Here''s the part most suppliers don''t think about. The couples who already booked you read your page too. When they see a new price, the question isn''t ''is it fair?'' It''s ''will mine change?''

Most won''t ask. They''ll just worry, and a worried couple is a couple who second-guesses every message from you until the day.

The kind thing is to answer before they ask: ''If you''ve booked, your price stays.''

On Setnayan that sentence is built in. When you change a card''s price, the app says it in plain words: couples who already booked keep their price; new bookings use the new price. Your booked couples don''t have to wonder, and you don''t have to write the reassurance message one couple at a time.

