  ('lib-1f62fdf01733145f1860180b', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Agree who decides, part by part', '11:52 p.m. ''Ate, I moved the toast to after dinner na lang.'' ⤵
She posted it in the family chat. The band read it. You didn''t.

Most micromanaging isn''t about trust. It starts where nobody agreed who decides what, so everyone decides everything.

On Setnayan, the hosts set, part by part, what their coordinator can edit, view or not see: guests, seats, schedule, suppliers, invitations, the Mood Board. Budget and payments are view-only for you, and the hosts book and pay. And when a supplier wants to change a time, they propose it and you decide, so the program doesn''t move behind your back.

One habit for your next client: in the first meeting, walk through each part together and agree who decides and who''s told. It''s much easier on day one than at 11:52 p.m. the night before.

