  ('lib-25e954fba9217f7f9511d03b', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Ask your suppliers before you announce', 'The church asks you to move one week later. The venue says yes. ⤵
Your photographer is already booked that day, for someone else.

When a date moves, hosts call the church and the venue first, because those feel like the hard parts. The suppliers they''ve already booked feel settled. But a booked supplier is booked for a day, not for a couple. The new Saturday might already belong to another family.

So the order matters: ask the people you''ve booked before you announce.

On Setnayan, a new date doesn''t go live until it''s checked against your booked suppliers. Pick a new date in your event''s details, and Setnayan checks the calendar of every supplier you''ve booked on the app. If it clashes for one of them, that supplier decides before the new date applies. It tells you who ("Your photography is booked elsewhere that day") and gives you a link to their chat, so you talk first and announce after.

