  ('lib-0f5a9f8c04f38833ece573a1', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Let the person paying see the quote', 'The couple chats with the caterer. Mama pays the caterer. ⤵
Mama has never seen the quote, only a screenshot of a screenshot.

In many Filipino events, the person planning and the person paying are different people: a parent paying for a debut, a tita paying the lechon, a ninong covering the band. The quote lives in one chat. The money comes from someone outside it.

So questions arrive late. "Ano ''yung ''crew meals''?" "Bakit may balance pa?" And the supplier answers the same quote twice, to two people, a week apart.

On Setnayan, the parent can be a co-host. Co-hosts plan with you and are in the supplier chat, so they read the same quote cards you do: the lines, the valid-until date and the payment plan. Nobody forwards a screenshot. Suppliers, it means the person paying hears it from you, once.

