  ('lib-5ab27d404099df58008512f9', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Every guest''s photos, in one place', 'Your photographer caught the vows. Your guests caught everything else. ⤵
The tito crying at the back. Lola dancing. The flower girl asleep under the table.

Those photos exist. They''re on dozens of phones, between a grocery receipt and a meme. A few reach you in the group chat, squashed and late. Most never do, not because anyone forgot to be kind, but because sending them is one more thing to do after a long night.

The moment you''ll want most in ten years might be on a phone you''ll never see.

Papic fixes that at the event itself. Guests point their phone at the event''s code and shoot, right from the browser: nothing to install, no account. No signal at the venue? Each photo saves on the phone and sends by itself when signal returns, while Papic is open. Guests can also add photos they took that day from their camera roll.

Every photo lands in one place, your Memories.

