  ('lib-c985b160d2c4d1769a4eeb30', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Every client''s event, one screen', 'It''s May. You have six events in six weeks, and six family group chats. ⤵
It isn''t the events that wear you out. It''s the switching.

Peak season burnout rarely comes from one hard wedding. It comes from forty small hunts a day: which chat had the new headcount, which list is the latest, which supplier asked about parking.

On Setnayan, ''Events you run'' puts every client''s event side by side on one screen, soonest first, each showing what needs you. When a client books you, their event''s dashboard opens for you on its own. You''re in every supplier chat, and time changes come to you to decide, so nothing is agreed behind your back.

It won''t make June shorter. It can make each day less scattered.

And one habit that helps either way: block one rest day a week on your calendar, like a booking.

