  ('lib-fbcd00b6e867bf6526230fd1', 'The Problem People Didn''t Know Existed · Answer the couple still waiting', 'Two couples asked about Saturday 14 August. You said yes to one. ⤵
The other is still waiting, and still planning around you.

It''s the quiet half of a double booking. Nothing is booked twice, so nothing feels wrong. But somewhere, a couple has your name on their list, hasn''t looked for anyone else, and is waiting for a reply that will be ''sorry po.''

The longer they wait, the fewer good suppliers are left for their date.

On Setnayan, the app won''t let that happen quietly. If other couples are still waiting on you for that date, it asks you to answer them first: "take one or turn the rest down — then come back and agree to this one. Nobody should be left hanging." And if the date already has as many bookings as you allow, the second yes is refused.

