  ('lib-a4b5e58ae594dcb037edf83f', 'Filipino tradition, the Setnayan way · Cord, veil and coins, explained', 'The veil goes over the bride''s head and the groom''s shoulder. Then the cord. ⤵

The cord and veil are among the most beautiful parts of a Filipino Catholic wedding. The veil says the two are clothed as one. The cord, looped in a figure eight, says the bond doesn''t end. Then the arras: coins the groom gives the bride as a promise to provide.

Each has its own pair of secondary sponsors. And every June, someone asks at the rehearsal: wait, who''s holding the cord?

On Setnayan, the entourage sits in your event: who''s the veil, who''s the cord, who''s the coin sponsor, and when they stand up.

