In a typhoon week, the coordinator often becomes the person everyone waits on. The kindest thing you can do is make the waiting shorter: set a decision time on Monday, decide on PAGASA''s and the local government''s advisories, and let the hosts make the final call with the options in front of them.

On Setnayan, if the hosts move the date, it''s checked against every booked supplier first; a supplier it clashes with decides before the new date applies. If the event goes ahead late, shift the schedule once and every supplier''s time moves with it.

The habit that helps most: ask every supplier now, before the storm, ''If we move, which dates can you do?'' Two or three dates from each turns a frightening decision into a short list the family can choose from.

