The teams that run smoothest in December decide one thing early: one person decides times, and everyone else carries messages. Assistants get one area each (the door, the stage, the suppliers, the family) and nobody changes the plan on their own.

The hard part is suppliers who don''t know that. The band talks to the bride''s tita. The caterer agrees a new time with the venue. And the coordinator finds out last.

On Setnayan, a booked coordinator is in every supplier chat on the event, so no supplier conversation happens without you. And when a supplier needs a different time, they propose it, and the coordinator decides. Nobody moves the program alone.

It doesn''t replace your briefing. It makes sure the briefing is the only version.

