  ('lib-15f5787bcb75e7dedeae2ffd', 'Problems of a Coordinator · Rush events: keep these four', '"Kaya pa po ba ang December? Six weeks na lang." ⤵
Every coordinator gets this call in September.

Rush events work when you decide early what''s non-negotiable. Keep: the venue, the food, a real headcount, and the papers, which take the longest (start them in week one). Cut or swap: anything with a long lead time, like custom printed items, imported details and a second outfit.

The other danger is the list itself. Six weeks of work squeezed into one feels like everything is urgent, and the truly urgent thing gets lost.

On Setnayan, Today shows what needs you, in order of urgency, and ''Do it tomorrow'' moves an item off your day without moving it for anyone else. And when the hosts book you as their coordinator, you get their own dashboard automatically: the guests, the schedule, the suppliers, all in one place.

