Here''s how it happens. You share one album link and ask everyone to add their photos. Guests open their camera roll and select everything from ''this week'': the reception, yes, but also the jeepney selfie from Tuesday, a forwarded ''Congrats!'' graphic, and a screenshot they meant to delete.

Nobody did anything wrong. A shared album simply takes whatever it''s given. Months later you''re scrolling your own wedding and hitting other people''s Tuesdays.

On Setnayan, guests can add photos from their camera roll to Papic, but only ones taken on the event day. The phone reads each file''s own taken-date, and anything without one, like screenshots and photos forwarded over chat, is left out. Your album stays your day, and only your day.

